  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Cast thy bread upon the waters: for thou shalt find it after many days.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 11:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Give a portion to seven, and also to eight; for thou knowest not what evil shall be upon the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 11:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "If the clouds be full of rain, they empty themselves upon the earth: and if the tree fall toward the south, or toward the north, in the place where the tree falleth, there it shall be.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 11:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "He that observeth the wind shall not sow; and he that regardeth the clouds shall not reap.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 11:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "As thou knowest not what is the way of the spirit, nor how the bones do grow in the womb of her that is with child: even so thou knowest not the works of God who maketh all.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 11:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "In the morning sow thy seed, and in the evening withhold not thine hand: for thou knowest not whether shall prosper, either this or that, or whether they both shall be alike good.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 11:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Truly the light is sweet, and a pleasant thing it is for the eyes to behold the sun:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 11:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "But if a man live many years, and rejoice in them all; yet let him remember the days of darkness; for they shall be many. All that cometh is vanity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 11:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Rejoice, O young man, in thy youth; and let thy heart cheer thee in the days of thy youth, and walk in the ways of thine heart, and in the sight of thine eyes: but know thou, that for all these things God will bring thee into judgment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 11:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Therefore remove sorrow from thy heart, and put away evil from thy flesh: for childhood and youth are vanity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 11:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:11:10"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
